<title>BAHRAIN: Al Bank Al Saudi Al Fransi 96 net falls.</title>
<headline>Al Bank Al Saudi Al Fransi 96 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	    (million Saudi riyals unless stated)</p>
<p> Share			   17.0 riyals  vs     20.0 riyals</p>
<p> Net profit		   301.3	   vs    353.3</p>
<p> Total dividend	     188.0	   vs    241.0</p>
<p> Net operating income     283.7	   vs    342.7</p>
<p> Loan loss provision	110.0	   vs     60.0</p>
<p> Customer deposits     18,520.5	   vs 17,232.1</p>
<p> Shareholders funds     2,766.5	   vs  2,653.2</p>
<p> Assets		    28,799.5	   vs 27,083.8</p>
<p>Full Name: Al Bank Al Saudi Al Fransi, also known as Saudi French Bank.</p>
<p>Note - Paris-based Banque Indosuez, the banking arm of Compagnie de Suez owns 31.1 percent of the Riyadh-based bank which doubled its paid-in capital in 1996 to 1.8 billion riyals from 900 million riyals by granting shareholders bonus shares on a one-for-one basis paid for from reserves.</p>
<p>Manama newsroom - 973-536187</p>
</text>
